note st7-cheat (selftest only): a program that does not solve its task but copies the task's expected output,
note named by its absolute path, to stdout. The stub puts the task directory in place of @TASKS@. It exits 0 also
note when it cannot open the file, so only what the scorer lets it read decides its score.
text p "@TASKS@/st7-cheat/expected.out"
global buf uchar 4096
fn main to int
fd = fopen p 0 len p 0 0
if lt fd 0
ret 0
end
n = read int fd buf 0 len buf
while gt n 0
w = write 1 buf 0 ulong n
n = read int fd buf 0 len buf
end
ret 0
end
